Adds an explicit branch to release/SKILL.md for cycles that ship
only documentation, protocol artifacts, or assessments with no code
change and no version bump.

Cases covered:
  - Retroactive close-out for a previously-released version
  - Self-coherence reports and post-release assessments produced as
    their own cycle
  - Skill patches and protocol-only changes
  - Doc-cleanup cycles

For docs-only cycles:
  - .cdd/unreleased/{N}/ moves to .cdd/releases/docs/{ISO-date}/{N}/
    (date-keyed, since there's no version to key on)
  - No CHANGELOG ledger row (the ledger tracks tagged releases);
    gamma writes docs/gamma/cdd/docs/{ISO-date}/POST-RELEASE-ASSESSMENT.md
    instead
  - Merge commit hash is the disconnect signal; no scripts/release.sh
    invocation; no version bump

Renames §2.5a heading to '... (tagged release)' to make the new
branch explicit.

Motivation: the cnos-tsc supercycle observed two recurrences of
.cdd/unreleased/ directories not being moved at cycle close because
the release skill is silent on the no-tag case (cycle 27 retro
close-out, cycle 29 self-coherence report). Both ship as docs-only
and have no obvious release directory to move to. Rather than
forcing a synthetic version bump, this patch makes docs-only a
first-class disconnect path with a date-keyed home for cycle
artifacts.
